# Ticket Lifecycle Management

## Context
This project is tracked via JSON files in the `ixdar-tickets/content` directory. A board summary at `ixdar-tickets/BOARD.md` is auto-generated by `ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py` via a Cursor `afterFileEdit` hook whenever any ticket file is modified.

## CRITICAL: Never Edit Ticket Files Directly
**DO NOT** use Write, StrReplace, or any file-editing tool on ticket JSON files (`ixdar-tickets/content/**/*.json` or `ixdar-tickets/done/**/*.json`). Direct edits bypass collision detection and have caused duplicate ticket IDs.

**ALL ticket mutations MUST go through the CLI:**
```
python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py <command>
```

## CLI Commands Reference

### Create a new ticket (auto-assigns next available ID)
```
python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py create \
  --epic IX --repo Ixdar \
  --title "Short title" \
  --description "Full description" \
  --subsystem automation geometry \
  --priority 3 \
  --blocked-by IX-2 IX-3 \
  --blocks IX-5 \
  --definition-of-done "Criteria..." \
  --testing-plan "Steps..." \
  --todo "First task" "Second task" \
  --unknown "Open question"
```

### Update an existing ticket
```
python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py update IX-3 \
  --status IN_PROGRESS \
  --add-changes "Implemented feature X" \
  --add-files "src/main/java/Foo.java" \
  --done-todos 0 2 \
  --add-todos "New follow-up task"
```

### Mark a ticket DONE (shorthand)
```
python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py mark done IX-3
```

### Get next available ID (for reference only; create handles this automatically)
```
python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py next-id IX
```

### Regenerate board / archive done tickets
```
python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py board
python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py archive
```

## Ticket JSON Schema (for reference, not for hand-editing)
- `id`, `title`, `description`, `epic` -- identity fields
- `repo` -- target repository name (e.g. `Ixdar`, `Blender-Procedural-Human`, `KriegEterna`, `ixdar-tickets`)
- `subsystem` -- array of IDs from `ixdar-tickets/subsystems.json`
- `status` -- one of `TODO`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `DONE`
- `priority` -- integer, lower = higher priority; do NOT change unless the user explicitly asks
- `blocked-by`, `blocks` -- dependency links
- `definition-of-done`, `testing-plan`, `todos`, `unknowns` -- planning fields
- `changes-made`, `related-files` -- tracking fields

## Automated Workflow
WHEN you perform a task that corresponds to a ticket ID (e.g., `IX-3`, `MESH-5`):

1. If you *started* work:
   ```
   python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py update IX-3 --status IN_PROGRESS
   ```
2. If you *completed* work:
   ```
   python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py mark done IX-3
   ```
3. To log changes, files, and completed todos:
   ```
   python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py update IX-3 \
     --add-changes "What was done" \
     --add-files "path/to/file.java" \
     --done-todos 0 1 2
   ```

## Examples
User: "I fixed the rendering bug in ENG-12."
Action: `python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py mark done ENG-12`

User: "I finished 3 TODO items in ENG-5."
Action: `python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py update ENG-5 --done-todos 0 1 2`

User: "Create a ticket for adding dark mode."
Action: `python ixdar-tickets/generate_board.py create --epic UI --repo Ixdar --title "Add dark mode" --description "..." --subsystem ui`
